  <div id="information-details">
    <div id="policy">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="row">
          <div class="col-md-12">
                <article>
                  <h2>Refund Policy</h2>
                  <hr/>
                  <p>Purchasing an extension or theme should give you confidence and value. If your purchase doesn’t meet expectations due to compatibility or technical issues, we offer a straightforward refund process.</p>
                  <h3>Refund Request Period</h3>
                  <p>You can request a refund within <strong>60 days</strong> of your purchase date. To begin the process, you’ll need to provide your <strong>Order ID</strong> as proof of purchase.</p>
                  <h3>Valid Reasons for Refund</h3>
                  <p>Refunds are granted in the following situations:</p>
                  <ul>
                    <li>The extension or theme is not compatible with your version of OpenCart.</li>
                    <li>The item is <strong>broken</strong>, does <strong>not work as described</strong>, or is <strong>non-functional</strong></li>
                    <li>The developer <strong>fails to respond or resolve issues</strong> during the active license/support period.</li>
                  </ul>
                  <p>Requests that do not meet these conditions may be declined.</p>
                  <h3>Developer Access Requirement</h3>
                  <p>To ensure issues are investigated and resolved thoroughly, customers must provide the developer with the necessary access to their server environment. This includes either:</p>
                  <ul>
                    <li>FTP access, or</li>
                    <li>cPanel (or equivalent server control panel) access</li>
                  </ul>
                  <p>This access allows the developer to diagnose and fix technical issues directly. If access is not provided, a refund will not be issued, provided the developer is able to resolve the issue once access is granted. By requesting support, you agree to cooperate with reasonable access requests to facilitate troubleshooting.</p>
                  <h3>How Refunds Are Processed</h3>
                  <p>Refunds are returned through the original payment method used at checkout:</p>
                  <ul>
                    <li><strong>Credit Card</strong>: Refunded directly to the same card. Even if the card is closed or inactive, the amount is returned to your card account.</li>
                    <li><strong>PayPal Balance or Bank Account</strong>: Refunded to your PayPal account.</li>
                    <li><strong>Split Payments (Card + PayPal Balance)</strong>: The credit card portion is returned to the card. The remaining amount goes back to your PayPal balance.</li>
                  </ul>
                  <p>Processing times depend on your payment provider.</p>
                  <h3>Need Help?</h3>
                  <p>If you have questions before requesting a refund, reach out to the developer or contact OpenCart support for assistance.</p>
                  <p><br/></p>
                  <p class="text-right"><small><i>Last Updated on 15 Jul, 2025</i></small></p>
                </article>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</div>
